      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "When a mayday call comes, every second counts. \n\nOn March 11, Station Boothbay Harbor responded to a sinking vessel 23 miles off the coast of Maine. The crew arrived on scene to find three mariners in the water.  \n\nWithin one minute, all three were safely aboard the USCG’s rescue boat. \n\nFor one of the rescued mariners, the thought of his family fueled his will to survive. \"I have a newborn baby, and I was thinking about getting home to my newborn,” he later shared. \n\nOutstanding work by our rescuers and supporting aircrews. As America’s maritime first responder, the Coast Guard is Always Ready to respond in crisis. \n\nRead more: https://t.co/yIbNZrohdT\n\n#SemperParatus",
      "text_resolved": "When a mayday call comes, every second counts. \n\nOn March 11, Station Boothbay Harbor responded to a sinking vessel 23 miles off the coast of Maine. The crew arrived on scene to find three mariners in the water.  \n\nWithin one minute, all three were safely aboard the USCG’s rescue boat. \n\nFor one of the rescued mariners, the thought of his family fueled his will to survive. \"I have a newborn baby, and I was thinking about getting home to my newborn,” he later shared. \n\nOutstanding work by our rescuers and supporting aircrews. As America’s maritime first responder, the Coast Guard is Always Ready to respond in crisis. \n\nRead more: https://bit.ly/4bE0iGz\n\n#SemperParatus",
